#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-1-how-to-run-a-model.ipynb:103
msgid ""
"First, we load the model that we wish to run from PyBaMM's model library. "
"For this notebook, we choose the Doyle-Fuller-Newman (DFN) model:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-1-how-to-run-a-model.ipynb:-1
msgid "[2]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-1-how-to-run-a-model.ipynb:-1
msgid "model = pybamm.lithium_ion.DFN()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-1-how-to-run-a-model.ipynb:124
msgid ""
"We now use this model to create a PyBaMM ``Simulation``, which is used to "
"process and solve the model:"
